LeanSearch v2 (https://github.com/frenzymath/LeanSearch-v2)
Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

The two-stage retrieval design used by the plan graph — an embedding stage that
recalls candidates, followed by a reranking stage that scores each (query,
candidate) pair — follows the shape introduced by LeanSearch v2. The reranker
instruction in `src/plan_store/rerank.py` is adapted from theirs.

Changes: the cross-encoder reranker (Qwen3-Reranker) is replaced with an OpenAI
LLM scoring candidates 0-10; the instruction is rewritten for plan-graph nodes
(informal content plus a formal anchor) rather than Mathlib declarations; and a
second instruction variant for informal research notes was added.

Paper: Gao, Sun, Jiang, Wang, Xu, Wu, Dai, Dong.
"LeanSearch v2: Global Premise Retrieval for Lean 4 Theorem Proving."
arXiv:2605.13137
